WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:08.590
Identify products based on their barcode with
Seeing AI.

00:00:08.590 --> 00:00:15.379
So Seeing AI plays audio cues to give you
an indication of when it first recognizes

00:00:15.379 --> 00:00:18.170
the possible presence of a barcode.

00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:22.920
The faster the beeps, the closer you are,
and then eventually you’ll hear a description

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:24.490
of what the product is.

00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:27.289
So for example, here I have a jar.

00:00:27.289 --> 00:00:32.780
I’m going to hold the phone over the jar,
parallel with it.

00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:34.650
Maybe one foot away.

00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:38.630
The distance to the object depends on how
big it is.

00:00:38.630 --> 00:00:42.180
The larger, the further away you would want
to be.

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:46.640
So, the phone is over the jar and I am not
hearing anything.

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:50.630
So let’s slowly rotated it until we hear
the beeps.

00:00:50.630 --> 00:00:55.970
&gt; (beeping)
There are other beeps, so let’s keep going.

00:00:55.970 --> 00:00:59.410
&gt; Processing
&gt; Barney Butter Barney and Company, Almond

00:00:59.410 --> 00:01:02.300
Butter Crunchy, button.

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:03.620
Cool!

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:04.620
Peanut butter.

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:06.220
I like that.

00:01:06.220 --> 00:01:08.890
Let’s try something else.

00:01:08.890 --> 00:01:11.260
So I have another product here.

00:01:11.260 --> 00:01:17.070
This time it is a box. and with a box, there
are six possible sides which I would have to

00:01:17.070 --> 00:01:19.040
scan.

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:23.350
In actual fact, it could be anywhere on those
six sides.

00:01:23.350 --> 00:01:29.700
So I am going to hold the phone quite a bit
further away this time so the camera can see

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:36.150
the entirety of one side at a time.

00:01:36.150 --> 00:01:39.250
So , we are not seeing anything on that side.

00:01:39.250 --> 00:01:40.270
And try another one.

00:01:40.270 --> 00:01:41.530
&gt; (Light beeping sound)
Woo!

00:01:41.530 --> 00:01:43.110
&gt; (Faster beeping sound)
That’s lucky!

00:01:43.110 --> 00:01:48.130
&gt; Annie’s Homegrown Microwavable Gluten
Free Mac &amp; cheese – 5 CT.

00:01:48.130 --> 00:01:49.150
Wow!

00:01:49.150 --> 00:01:50.170
Great!

00:01:50.170 --> 00:01:55.100
So mac and cheese, and I was lucky i got it
on the second side this time.

00:01:55.100 --> 00:01:59.680
So to recap, we use bar codes to identify
what a product is.

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:05.729
Hold the phone over the object you want to
recognize, maybe about a foot away.

00:02:05.729 --> 00:02:09.500
But you should try different distances based
on the size.

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:14.749
Make sure the phone is parallel, and start
rotating the object until you hear the beeps.

00:02:14.749 --> 00:02:19.950
Make slight adjustments until the beeping
gets faster and you hear the description read

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:20.970
out.

00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:26.810
Sometimes, you’ll hear that more information
is available, like the instructions on the

00:02:26.810 --> 00:02:27.950
package.

00:02:27.950 --> 00:02:32.239
Now, I better get back to putting away my
groceries.

00:02:32.239 --> 00:02:33.739
Microsoft logo appears

